---
import LinkCards from '../components/LinkCards.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const discussions = 'https://github.com/tachyon-cms/tachyoncms/discussions';
const issues =
  'https://github.com/tachyon-cms/tachyoncms/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22%2C%22help+wanted%22';

const next = [
  ['Rich text and blocks', 'Long-form writing with code samples and tables, and pages built from reusable sections.'],
  ['Drafts, versions and scheduled publishing', "So nothing goes live before it's meant to."],
  ['Media', 'Upload once, reuse anywhere, with responsive images.'],
  ['Live preview', "Look at a draft before it's published."],
  ['Authoring tools', 'Markdown in and out, and bulk import.'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Roadmap · TachyonCMS"
  description="What TachyonCMS does today, the order the rest is being built in, and where you can change that order."
  path="/roadmap"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Roadmap"
    title="What's next, and in what order"
    lede="The developer half shipped in v0.1.0. Everything an editor touches comes next, and the order is set by one goal: running this site on TachyonCMS itself."
  />

  <div class="roadmap">
    <Prose split>
      <h2 id="today">Works today</h2>
      <p>
        Content types defined over the API or kept in a JSON file you diff and apply. Twenty-odd field types, including
        relationships, groups, arrays and map points. Filters that reach through relationships and into lists, joins,
        and <code>select</code> and <code>populate</code> so you fetch only what you need. Sign-in with sessions or
        bearer tokens, scoped API keys, roles, and access rules down to a single field.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's <a href="/releases">v0.1.0</a>, and it's pre-alpha. The{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/tachyon-cms/tachyoncms/blob/v0.1.0/README.md#what-works-today">README</a> has the
        full list, with examples.
      </p>

      <h2 id="next">Being built, in this order</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        {
          next.map(([title, text], i) => (
            <li>
              <h3>
                {title}
                {i === 0 && <span class="pill">Under way</span>}
              </h3>
              <p>{text}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p>
        After those comes the admin screen. The bar for it: anyone who has used WordPress can pick it up without
        training. <a href="/product/admin">Here's what it's being built on.</a>
      </p>
      <p>None of this is in v0.1.0, and none of it has a date. What you're looking at is the order.</p>

      <h2 id="say">Think the order's wrong?</h2>
      <p>
        I'd much rather hear it now than after it ships. Two polls are open, and the roadmap itself started as a
        discussion you can reply to.
      </p>
      <LinkCards
        links={[
          {
            href: `${discussions}/39`,
            title: 'Vote on what comes next',
            text: 'Drafts, media, live preview, Markdown import, the admin or GraphQL: which do you need first?',
          },
          {
            href: `${discussions}/38`,
            title: 'Pick the first starter',
            text: 'Astro, Next.js, SvelteKit, Nuxt, Remix or React Router, or something else. The winner gets built first.',
          },
          { href: `${discussions}/35`, title: 'Reply to the roadmap', text: 'Discussion #35, where this page started.' },
        ]}
      />
      <p>
        Rather build than vote? I've opened <a href={issues}>a set of issues</a> that are ready to pick up. Each one says which files to
        change, how to test it, and when it's done. Say you're taking one, and it's yours.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .roadmap {
    padding: 64px 0 clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }
  .roadmap :global(.prose > h2:first-child) {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  /* Ruled rows, numbered in the margin. */
  .steps {
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }
  .steps li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 16px 0 16px 40px;
    counter-increment: step;
  }
  .steps li + li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
  }
  .steps li:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .steps li::before {
    content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
    position: absolute;
    top: 19px;
    left: 0;
    font: 400 12.5px/1.4 var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--c-muted);
  }
  .steps li:first-child::before {
    top: 3px;
    color: var(--c-blue-soft);
  }
  .steps h3 {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px 12px;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .steps p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
